# Core infrastructure

Place types under `org.devbot.bookmymovie.core`:

```text
persistence/   BaseEntity, AuditableEntity, JpaConfig
security/      Role, Permission, RolePermissions  — no GrantedAuthority
cache/         RedisConfig          — when Redis is introduced
messaging/     KafkaConfig          — only if we actually use Kafka
config/        other cross-cutting Spring config
```

Add Redis/Kafka **starters on `core`** only when those classes exist. Do not scaffold unused config.

```java
// GOOD — mapped superclass for every feature entity
package org.devbot.bookmymovie.core.persistence;
@MappedSuperclass
public abstract class BaseEntity {}

// BAD — movie table in core
package org.devbot.bookmymovie.core.persistence;
@Entity
public class Movie {}
```

Keep out of `core`: `@RestController`, feature `@Service`, `GrantedAuthority`, `SecurityFilterChain`, Flyway SQL, `application.properties`. Seat-lock use cases stay in `booking`; core only supplies Redis/JPA plumbing and domain role/permission types.
